diff --git a/docs/deployment.md b/docs/deployment.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d4b3ce1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+## Deploy on one Linux server with Kamal
+
+The OSS deployment in `config/deploy.yml` runs the web app and Solid Queue
+background jobs in **one container**. It uses SQLite and local Active Storage;
+there is no separate database, Redis, or jobs server. This is separate from the
+SaaS deployment under `saas/`.
+
+1. Provide a Linux server with Docker, SSH access (by default as `root`), and
+   ports 80 and 443 open. Point a DNS A/AAAA record for your hostname at it.
+   Install Ruby and Bundler on your workstation and run `bundle install`.
+   Have a Docker Hub account and a repository for the image (private or public).
+2. Edit `config/deploy.yml`: replace `fizzy.example.com` (once, at the YAML
+   anchor), `your-dockerhub-user` in **both** `image` and `registry.username`,
+   and the SMTP host, port, username, and `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`. The from
+   address should be authorized by your SMTP provider. The example uses
+   authenticated SMTP with STARTTLS on port 587. Set `builder.arch` to `arm64`
+   if both the build machine and server are ARM, or configure a compatible
+   Kamal builder. `WEB_CONCURRENCY` defaults to 2 to suit a small box.
+3. Run `cp .kamal/secrets.example .kamal/secrets` and replace all three values
+   there. Use a Docker Hub access token for `KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD`; generate
+   `SECRET_KEY_BASE` with `bin/rails secret` or `openssl rand -hex 64` and keep
+   it unchanged on future deploys. Enter your SMTP account password. Do **not**
+   commit `.kamal/secrets` (it is gitignored).
+4. Run `bin/kamal setup` from your workstation. Kamal builds and pushes the
+   image, installs the proxy, obtains a TLS certificate for the configured
+   hostname, and starts the app at `https://your-host`. The DNS record and
+   inbound ports must work for certificate issuance. Subsequent releases use
+   `bin/kamal deploy`.
+
+The Docker image runs as UID 1000. Kamal's named `fizzy_storage` Docker volume
+is mounted at `/rails/storage`, which is owned by that UID in the image. It
+holds **all** SQLite databases (including queue, cable, and cache) and uploaded
+files. `bin/docker-entrypoint` prepares the databases on app startup, and Puma
+runs Solid Queue in-process. Keep and back up the volume, including SQLite WAL
+files: deleting the volume, running `docker volume prune`, or moving to another
+server without copying it will lose data. Back up from a consistent snapshot
+(or stop the app first); the image and subsequent deployments do not replace
+that volume. Mail must work to receive sign-in codes.
diff --git a/test/deployment/one_box_test.rb b/test/deployment/one_box_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e9ee062
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/deployment/one_box_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+require "minitest/autorun"
+require "yaml"
+
+class OneBoxTest < Minitest::Test
+  def setup
+    @deploy = YAML.load_file(File.expand_path("../../config/deploy.yml", __dir__), aliases: true)
+  end
+
+  def test_one_web_container_with_proxy_tls_and_persistent_storage
+    assert_equal "fizzy", @deploy.fetch("service")
+    assert_equal 1, @deploy.fetch("servers").fetch("web").size
+    assert_equal true, @deploy.fetch("proxy").fetch("ssl")
+    assert_equal @deploy.fetch("proxy").fetch("host"), @deploy.fetch("env").fetch("clear").fetch("APP_HOST")
+    assert_equal 80, @deploy.fetch("proxy").fetch("app_port")
+    assert_includes @deploy.fetch("volumes"), "fizzy_storage:/rails/storage"
+    refute @deploy.fetch("servers").key?("jobs")
+    assert_equal "2", @deploy.fetch("env").fetch("clear").fetch("WEB_CONCURRENCY").to_s
+  end
+
+  def test_mail_and_secrets
+    clear = @deploy.fetch("env").fetch("clear")
+    secrets = @deploy.fetch("env").fetch("secret")
+    %w[ SMTP_HOST SMTP_PORT SMTP_USERNAME MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS ].each { |name| assert clear.key?(name), name }
+    %w[ SECRET_KEY_BASE SMTP_PASSWORD ].each { |name| assert_includes secrets, name }
+    production = File.read(File.expand_path("../../config/environments/production.rb", __dir__))
+    assert_includes production, 'ENV["APP_HOST"]'
+    assert_includes production, 'ENV["SMTP_HOST"]'
+  end
+end
